# Gitignored files Claude Code copies into every worktree it creates.
# .gitignore syntax; a pattern only takes effect for a file that is BOTH
# matched here and ignored by git — tracked files come with the checkout.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so without this the dev server dies in
# src/proxy.ts with "Your project's URL and Key are required to create a
# Supabase client!" and every gate that reads env vars fails without naming
# the cause.
#
# This is the first line of defence; .claude/hooks/bootstrap-worktree.sh is the
# second. The hook symlinks .env.local at session start but leaves an existing
# file alone, so a copy made here wins and the hook only covers worktrees made
# some other way (plain `git worktree add`). The trade: a copy is a snapshot,
# so a rotated key reaches a copied worktree only when the file is replaced.

# Local environment — Supabase keys, site URL, the EYES_ON_* verifier account.
.env.local

# Deliberately NOT listed:
#   node_modules/                 a copied or linked tree panics Turbopack — run `npm ci`
#   .next/                        build output, regenerated
#   .claude/settings.local.json   one person's permission allowlist
#   .claude/launch.json           points at its own worktree's paths
